# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
#
# Cloudflare Pages does NOT send Access-Control-Allow-Origin by default. Verified 2026-09-15:
# static assets on Cloudflare Pages sites without a _headers file return no CORS header at all.
# This file is what supplies it, so deleting it silently breaks every browser-based XLS-26
# consumer while the site itself keeps looking fine.
#
# GitHub Pages ignores this file entirely - it sends Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on everything
# and offers no way to configure headers. If you deploy there, the CORS rule below is redundant
# but harmless, and the Content-Type rule below cannot be honoured.
#
# Format: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# Limits: 100 rules, 2,000 characters per line.
#
# After any host or DNS change, verify rather than assume:
#     cd site && npm run verify:live -- pondprotocol.pages.dev
#
# The path-specific block below is what covers /.well-known/xrp-ledger.toml.
# XLS-26 asks for Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * and accepts text/plain or
# application/toml. text/plain is the usual XLS-26 choice; this rule sets it.
#
# A note from real-world observation: a malformed line in a _headers file can stop later rules
# from applying, and the deploy still succeeds. Header rules are not verified until you fetch the
# response. Always check the live response, never just the file.

# XLS-26 requires this file to be readable cross-origin. This is the single most important rule
# in this file: without it, wallets that resolve token metadata in the browser cannot read it.
/.well-known/xrp-ledger.toml
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Anything else under .well-known/ should also be publicly readable.
/.well-known/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Ordinary hardening for the documentation pages. No inline script, no third-party anything, so
# the policy can be strict.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; script-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
